{\plain {\fs24 ENEE 425     Project 3\par 
Frequency Modulation (FM) with Phase-Locked
 Loop (PLL) Demodulation\par Due 3/14/96}}
}
.TXT 10 0 175 0
Cg a71.100000,73.000000,310
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain {An alternative to modulating a 
signal by varying the amplitude of the carrier,
 amplitude modulation, is varying the frequency
 of the carrier, frequency modulation.  
One popular method of demodulating an FM
 signal is the phase-locked loop.  Such 
a modulation-demodulation scheme is what
 we will study here.}}
}
.TXT 11 0 143 0
Cg a42.700000,69.000000,69
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain {First we d}{efine the signal in
 time and its frequency modulation.}}
}
