0 1 44 19 0 3 Discrim. Error with for. and back diff.
.TXT 31 -7 335 0
Cg a73.300000,73.000000,528
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain Evidently, as G increases, the magnitude
 of the error between the estimated and 
original signal decreases while the noise,
 which can be seen as the "unsmoothness"
 of the curves, increases.  Conversely, 
when G is small, the error is large but 
the signal noise is small, which can be 
seen by the smoothness of the graph.  Also,
 the unstablizing effect of the forward 
difference is very easy to see, as the signal
 estimate using the forward difference contains
 gross error in comparison with the backwards
 difference estimate.}
}
